# Privacy on the web surfaces

`codify-web` binds to `127.0.0.1`, has no authentication, refuses
cross-origin POSTs, and keeps nothing on disk.

The Pages site runs Python in the browser via Pyodide served from the
site. Add no third-party script, font, or analytics hosts to the site
build or to `codify-web`. Both use the system font stack.

CSP `connect-src` may include only `'self'`, the three opt-in cloud AI
origins (`https://api.anthropic.com`, `https://api.openai.com`,
`https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com`), and
`http://localhost:11434` / `http://127.0.0.1:11434`.

Privacy chrome (no new third-party requests, no policy upload) is not
negotiable for a prettier layout. Tests that lock this:
`tests/test_webapp.py`, `tests/test_site.py`, `tests/test_local_assets.py`.
